Make rpfolio print each file's size when receiving from the Portfolio

The Portfolio sends a file's size before the file itself, and rpfolio
already reads it into `total`, but never prints it. This prints it as
"File size: N bytes." so PiPortfolioDaemon can show exact download
progress from the start. Without it, the size of a file larger than
one 28 KB block is estimated until its last block starts.

Applies to https://github.com/skudi/transfolio at commit ab89073:

    git checkout ab89073
    git apply ~/PiPortfolioDaemon/extras/rpfolio-file-size.patch

diff --git a/transfolio.c b/transfolio.c
index ca34608..37526f2 100644
--- a/transfolio.c
+++ b/transfolio.c
@@ -718,6 +718,7 @@ void receiveFile(const char * source, const char * dest) {
 		}
 
 		total = controlData[7] + ((int)controlData[8] << 8) + ((int)controlData[9] << 16);
+		printf("File size: %d bytes.\n", total);
 
 		if (total > blocksize) {
 			printf("Transmission consists of %d blocks of payload.\n", (total+blocksize-1)/blocksize);
